raw_json:
{"skill": "Function of Sentence", "difficulty": "Medium", "question": "In an article examining the impact of digital technology on modern communication, the author discusses both the empowering benefits and the unforeseen challenges of online connectivity. One particular sentence reads: 

"Yet, paradoxically, the very networks designed to empower us have, in some cases, undermined our ability to filter and verify facts." 

What is the primary function of this sentence in the context of the passage?", "choices": ["A. It contrasts the potential benefits of digital networks with their negative side effects.", "B. It introduces a counterargument by highlighting an ironic twist in the expected outcomes of digital networks.", "C. It provides detailed evidence to support the benefits of technological advancements.", "D. It restates previously mentioned ideas to summarize the overall argument."], "answer": "B", "explanation": "The sentence uses the term "paradoxically" to signal an unexpected contradiction: although digital networks are designed to empower users, they also have the unintended effect of compromising our ability to critically assess information. This counterpoint challenges the solely positive view of technology and serves to introduce a more nuanced discussion in the passage."}

